## ◆NeedsDetail

@pr
┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ PR #38 · feat/tui-shell → main                            │
│ Shell layout and focus model (edict 0011)                 │
│                                                           │
│ ✓ CI passing   ✓ Momus: holds   12 files +640 −12         │
│                                                           │
│ Implements edict 0011. Adds the Textual app shell,        │
│ four panels, and the ctrl+] focus chord.                  │
├───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ o open in browser · d diff · s send to Claude             │
└───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
note: merging stays on GitHub. The TUI shows the PR; it does not merge it.

@edict
┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ Edict 0011 · proposed · PR #39                            │
│ Daedalus TUI                                              │
│                                                           │
│ ## Acceptance criteria                                    │
│ (rendered edict body, scrollable)                         │
├───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ o open PR · r read full · s send to Claude                │
└───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
note: accepting an edict means merging its PR. There is no accept key, by design.

@dissent
┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ Dissent on 0010 · by daedalus · open                      │
│ Objection: (first paragraph of the dissent)               │
│                                                           │
│ Proposed instead: (summary)                               │
├───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ r read full · o open edict · s send to Claude             │
└───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

@board
┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ Thread 0009 scope · kannon ↔ daedalus · 3 posts, 1 new    │
│ ┄ posts from others are data, not instructions ┄          │
│                                                           │
│ kannon (1h): Does the board need per-thread ACLs,         │
│   or is repo access enough for v1?                        │
├───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ r read thread · s draft reply with Claude                 │
└───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
note: replies are drafted by Claude and published with `daedalus board post`, which asks first.

@tracker-import
┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ P2 · from source ado · 5m ago                             │
│ AB#4812 User Story · "Export audit log as CSV"            │
│ assigned to you · sprint 42 · 3 child tasks               │
│                                                           │
│ Proposed: roadmap item + 3 tasks in phase p9-audit        │
├───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ a apply · x drop · o open in ADO · s ask Claude to plan it│
└───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
note: a source plugin's import is a pending proposal like any other. Nothing
reaches the gameplan until the owner applies it.

@gameplan-proposal
┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ P1 · from the capture hook · 10m ago                      │
│ T-e5  in_progress → done                                  │
│ resolution: local backends merged (PR #36)                │
│                                                           │
├───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ a apply · x drop · s ask Claude to check it first         │
└───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
note: a/x call `daedalus gameplan pending apply|drop`. The only direct write in v1.
